! high_mass_h2_pilot fixed-ctau ATLAS response card: pp -> H2 H2 -> b b~ b b~,
! m_H2 = 250.0 GeV, ctau FORCED to the mH=150 benchmark value
! 4.326221529733112 mm (this point's own physical ctau_physical_mm is many orders of
! magnitude smaller -- see docs/campaigns/high_mass_h2_physical_point_scan_v1/
! high_mass_valid_points.csv in the dihiggs repo -- and is NOT used here by
! design: this is the FACTORIZED_G_ONLY / MASS_CONTROL response study, which
! isolates the mH2 dependence of the ATLAS Trackless response at fixed
! response lifetime, per HIGH_MASS_H2_CONTRACT.md section 4 / mission section 9).
! Extends results/mass_dependence_trackless/ (mH=130/150/170) to a new,
! theory-valid high-mass point beyond the diagnostic-only range. Every
! setting other than the mass-dependent production sample and 35:m0 is
! copied unchanged from cards/mass_dependence_trackless/fixed_ctau_mH130_run_01.cmnd
! (shower, jet definition, analysis mode, lifetime mechanism, relabel
! mechanism), which is itself copied unchanged from
! cards/r8_h2_model_derived_4b/physical_run_01.cmnd except mass/LHE path.
! point_id = point_0960bd688a662562 (dihiggs-point-search science/high-mass-valid-point-atlas, commit fa19d06)
!
! Production kinematics: g g > H > h2 h2, sqrt(s) = 13 TeV, MadGraph 3.5.3,
! dihiggs_hep_cross results/r14_direct_g_production, run tag s101
! (10000 events generated; the first 1000 are extracted as a genuine
! 1000-event LHE slice via scripts/slice_lhe.py -- no MadGraph
! regeneration -- matching R8/mass_dependence_trackless per-seed statistics
! exactly. r8_geometry_driver enforces an exact-event-count invariant on its
! input, which is why a true 1000-event file is used rather than
! truncating via Main:numberOfEvents alone.)
!   raw LHE sha256     = c6c3292715b6a961e50c47f3542ec1c3bdaf209d24b4e6141d2cb54d73761198
!   sliced LHE sha256  = e41876662ff05321d2df6e19b6a784abc1cbaac7015daca32d9221d3865c6d38
!   relabelled sha256  = 13c91b07b4259350cc01ced763efc4bcddccd87e161a9af30443f2c17d724176
!
! Relabel mechanism (9000006 -> 35, scripts/relabel_lhe_pdg.py) is byte-for-byte
! the same validated tool used for R8/mass_dependence_trackless;
! momenta/status/mothers/colours/mass/tau/spin are unchanged, only the IDUP
! field differs (2000 changes per run of 1000 events; verified
! by the script's own acceptance check).
!
! Shower configuration (FSR on, ISR on, MPI off, hadronization on, Tune:pp =
! 21), jet definition (FastJet kt, R=0.4, pT>20 GeV, unmodified
! Simpler_ToyDetector.cc), and the original/published Trackless analysis mode
! are reused unchanged from the R8/R7/mass_dependence_trackless real-recast
! path. The later `modified` Trackless analysis is NOT used here. The
! published ATLAS thresholds themselves are NOT modified by this card --
! only the input sample changes.
Main:numberOfEvents = 1000
Main:timesAllowErrors = 3
Init:showChangedSettings = on
Init:showChangedParticleData = off
Next:numberCount = 5000
Next:numberShowInfo = 0
Next:numberShowProcess = 0
Next:numberShowEvent = 0

Random:setSeed = on
Random:seed = 81005

PartonLevel:MPI = off
PartonLevel:ISR = on
PartonLevel:FSR = on
HadronLevel:Hadronize = on
Tune:pp = 21

Higgs:useBSM = on
35:m0 = 250.0
35:mMin = 100.
35:tauCalc = off
35:tau0 = 4.326221529733112
35:onMode = off
35:onIfMatch = 5 -5

Recast:llpPdgIds = {35}
Recast:llpTau0 = 4.326221529733112
LesHouches:setLifetime = 2

Beams:frameType = 4
LHEFInputs:nSubruns = 1
Main:subrun = 0
Beams:LHEF = data/raw/high_mass_h2_pilot/relabelled_mH250_s101.lhe.gz
